      "offsets": {
        "from": 0,
        "to": 5040
      },
      "text": " Let's walk through the retail data workbench, built for the AI engineering track."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:05,040",
        "to": "00:00:09,360"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 5040,
        "to": 9360
      },
      "text": " The browser, API and batch evaluator use one Python service."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:09,360",
        "to": "00:00:13,760"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 9360,
        "to": 13760
      },
      "text": " I'll load two sample files, an order line table and a product catalog."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:13,760",
        "to": "00:00:18,240"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 13760,
        "to": 18240
      },
      "text": " Each run preserves the original bytes under a generated identifier."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:18,240",
        "to": "00:00:22,720"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 18240,
        "to": 22720
      },
      "text": " A cleaned version appears only after the service verifies the row count and headers."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:22,720",
        "to": "00:00:26,240"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 22720,
        "to": 26240
      },
      "text": " The order's file starts with five rows."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:26,240",
        "to": "00:00:30,720"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 26240,
        "to": 30720
      },
      "text": " The workbench profiles the original and builds the cleaning plan before applying it."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:30,720",
        "to": "00:00:35,040"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 30720,
        "to": 35040
      },
      "text": " Each step includes its fields, reason, risk and number of affected rows."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:35,040",
        "to": "00:00:42,240"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 35040,
        "to": 42240
      },
      "text": " In this case the cleaner trims the region normalizes declared prices and keeps SKU001 as text."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:42,240",
        "to": "00:00:47,040"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 42240,
        "to": 47040
      },
      "text": " A date that might mean March 4th or April 3rd remains in the dataset and is listed as an"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:47,040",
        "to": "00:00:51,200"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 47040,
        "to": 51200
      },
      "text": " unresolved parse failure. Both original and clean files can be downloaded."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:52,640",
        "to": "00:00:58,640"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 52640,
        "to": 58640
      },
      "text": " Next I ask which store is best? West could mean sales, return rate or another measure."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:58,640",
        "to": "00:01:03,840"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 58640,
        "to": 63840
      },
      "text": " The assistant asks for a metric or an appropriate column. It leaves the conversation scope alone"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:03,840",
        "to": "00:01:09,280"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 63840,
        "to": 69280
      },
      "text": " while the question is unresolved. For the next example I'll start a fresh conversation with a precise scope."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:09,280",
        "to": "00:01:16,480"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 69280,
        "to": 76480
      },
      "text": " I ask to consider only stores in the west. The workbench reports four eligible order lines and"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:16,480",
        "to": "00:01:21,440"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 76480,
        "to": 81440
      },
      "text": " saves that filter. Then I ask which categories had the highest return rate among those."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:21,440",
        "to": "00:01:27,040"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 81440,
        "to": 87040
      },
      "text": " The plan carries forward west and joins order lines to the product catalog by SKU."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:27,040",
        "to": "00:01:30,720"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 87040,
        "to": 90720
      },
      "text": " The service checks that the catalog is unique on that key before joining."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:30,720",
        "to": "00:01:36,800"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 90720,
        "to": 96800
      },
      "text": " And here's the answer. A parallel at 60% that three units returned out of five sold."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:36,800",
        "to": "00:01:41,280"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 96800,
        "to": 101280
      },
      "text": " The evidence panel shows the version filter join cardinality, row count and operation."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:41,280",
        "to": "00:01:43,920"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 101280,
        "to": 103920
      },
      "text": " The numerator and denominator are in the full trees."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:43,920",
        "to": "00:01:48,960"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 103920,
        "to": 108960
      },
      "text": " For another follow-up I ask which status has the most records?"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:48,960",
        "to": "00:01:51,840"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 108960,
        "to": 111840
      },
      "text": " The service groups by status and counts rows."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:51,840",
        "to": "00:01:56,800"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 111840,
        "to": 116800
      },
      "text": " Completed has three. The conversation reloads with both the answers and their evidence."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:01:56,800",
        "to": "00:02:02,880"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 116800,
        "to": 122880
      },
      "text": " Doug DB executes an allowed listed parameterized plan. The language model when enabled only"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:02,880",
        "to": "00:02:08,560"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 122880,
        "to": 128560
      },
      "text": " proposes that plan. It never sees CSV cells or computes the final number. This run uses the"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:08,560",
        "to": "00:02:14,640"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 128560,
        "to": 134640
      },
      "text": " credential free planner. Now I upload a CSV whose data row has too many fields."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:14,640",
        "to": "00:02:20,000"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 134640,
        "to": 140000
      },
      "text": " The run fails with the affected line number. The failed run has no published cleaned artifact"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:20,000",
        "to": "00:02:25,440"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 140000,
        "to": 145440
      },
      "text": " and previous runs are still in history. That failure path also appears in the headless evaluator"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:25,440",
        "to": "00:02:30,320"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 145440,
        "to": 150320
      },
      "text": " between two successful cases. So our reviewer can verify case isolation without the browser."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:30,320",
        "to": "00:02:35,840"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 150320,
        "to": 155840
      },
      "text": " Finally I reload the valid sample and ask for revenue by category."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:02:35,840",
        "to": "00:02:40,400"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 155840,
